<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Opuntian Locris</h1><p class="st-meta">700 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.) · capital Opus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Confederation of the eastern Locrians on the Euboean Gulf, centred on Opus and remembered for the Locrian maidens sent to Troy.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locrians">Locrians</a> lived along the coast of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euboea">Euboea</a>, separated from their western kin in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ozolian-locris">Ozolian Locris</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doris-greece">Doris</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocis">Phocis</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a> placed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajax-the-lesser">Ajax the Lesser</a> among them. By the Archaic period their towns formed a confederation led by Opus, governed by an oligarchic council of a thousand.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locrians">Locrians</a> kept old customs, such as sending two noble maidens each year to serve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena">Athena</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Ilion</a> in atonement for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajax-the-lesser">Ajax</a>'s sacrilege. An early 5th century BCE bronze tablet records the terms for Locrian colonists at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafpaktos">Naupactus</a>. They fought with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonidas-i">Leonidas</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-thermopylae">Thermopylae</a> in 480 BCE, then were forced to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a>, and later usually sided with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sparta">Sparta</a> against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/phocian-league">Phocian League</a> overran much of the region in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-sacred-war">Third Sacred War</a>. Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locris">Locris</a> later passed under Macedonian, Boeotian and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aetolian-league">Aetolian League</a> control and came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 146 BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 700 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:45.77%;width:11.02%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>700 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Opus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Locrian Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Greece</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Eastern Locris, Opus</dd></dl></aside></div>

